---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="About — Harrison Mohr"
  description="Applied AI engineer building production AI agent systems. From audio production to ML engineering."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-8 sm:gap-12 mb-12">
      <div class="shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/headshot.png"
          alt="Harrison Mohr"
          class="w-36 h-36 rounded-full object-cover"
          width="144"
          height="144"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-1">Harrison Mohr</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted mb-4">Applied AI Engineer</p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/jackharrisonmohr"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="hover:text-accent transition-colors"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://linkedin.com/in/harrisonmohr"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="hover:text-accent transition-colors"
          >
            LinkedIn
          </a>
          <a
            href="mailto:jackharrisonmohr@gmail.com"
            class="hover:text-accent transition-colors"
          >
            jackharrisonmohr@gmail.com
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p>
        I'm a founding engineer at <a href="https://maketimeflow.com">MakeTimeFlow</a>,
        where I build production AI agent systems — voice-enabled coaching, LLM
        orchestration, and real-time integrations — on a small team shipping fast.
        I own the full product lifecycle, from customer research and product
        strategy through architecture and deployment.
      </p>

      <p>
        Before this, I led engineering on two NSF-funded ML platforms at the
        University of Houston, where I owned the full AWS stack and bridged the
        gap between ML model outputs and user-facing applications. One of those
        platforms powered emergency food distribution logistics for the Houston
        Food Bank. Before that, I built deep learning training pipelines for
        medical imaging research at UChicago's Department of Radiology, where I
        led a small team developing segmentation models for renal cell carcinoma
        detection.
      </p>

      <p>
        My path into engineering wasn't conventional. I studied audio design and
        production at Columbia College Chicago, where I wrote and produced music
        that's since accumulated over two million views on YouTube. That
        background gave me an obsession with signal quality, careful listening,
        and building things that work in the real world — instincts that
        transferred directly when I pivoted to computer science and earned my
        M.A.S. at Illinois Institute of Technology.
      </p>

      <p>
        I care about shipping AI systems that actually work in production,
        building infrastructure that scales beyond the demo, and making rigorous
        engineering decisions under real constraints. I'm drawn to problems at
        the intersection of AI capabilities and production reliability — where
        the model is only part of the system, and the system is what matters.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
